WEBVTT

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:09.730
Senpai!

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.200
Ugh, this place stinks like a hospital.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.600
It is a hospital.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.410
Welcome back to the waking world.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.240
Ryuuka.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.580
Ryuuka!

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.740
Ryuuka!

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.380
Shimizudani-senpai wouldn't leave 
you until a little while ago,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.290
but the fifth players' match is coming up,

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.670
so we had to pry her away.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.680
That's too bad.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.680
I'll just have to tough it out.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.430
So it's already the fifth players' match.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.000
I must've been asleep for a long time.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.490
How are you feeling?

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.190
Who put this hospital gown on me? It's tight.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.110
But if I blacked out again,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.960
maybe it means I can see 
one hundred turns ahead now.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.620
Where did you get that number from?

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.150
<b>Intensify</b>

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.370
Should I turn the TV on?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.250
Yeah, I want to see Ryuuka!

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.850
<i>We're in the last hand of 
the fourth players' match</i>

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.460
<i>and three of the players are already in tenpai!</i>

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.090
Which team will take the win 
to the fifth players' match?!

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.670
Yeah, Sagimori's play does resemble hers.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.510
Huh?

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.100
Her playing style resembles that of 
Akado, who I played ten years ago.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.850
Oh, speaking of Akado, 
she's now Achiga's coach!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.710
Tsumo!

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.650
700. 1,300.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.530
The match is over!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.640
Shiraitodai barely holds on to first place as they

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.620
move to the fifth players' match!

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.530
Yeah!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.710
I'm warmed up now!

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.640
I got up to 100 gears!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.130
That makes you warmer?

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.880
Shizu, you're the only high school who'd be

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.990
happy about a silly number like 100.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.190
You're not a boy in grade school, you know.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.510
Leave this to me!

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.770
I'll go settle this right—

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.400
Wait!

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.020
Senriyama's Eguchi Sera...

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.200
Remember how she looked at Hamanako?

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.640
The bus is about to leave!

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.020
Not at all!

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.460
She usually wears a boy's uniform, 
even during interviews,

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.910
but during a match, she always 
wears a proper girl's uniform.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.200
My point is, you need to 
put on your uniform too!

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:57.560
All right!

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.920
Now I'm really ready to go.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:00.750
Yeah!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.640
Good luck!

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.180
Give it your best.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.540
I will!

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:08.890
Arata-san!

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.480
Good work.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.480
You're wearing a uniform?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.550
I had to borrow it from Ako.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:19.580
Wearing this really makes me 
feel like I'm an Achiga student.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.360
Except you've always been one...

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.030
Well, good luck.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.290
<i>The rest is up to you, Achiga's fifth player.</i>

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:32.880
<i>Yes.</i>

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.570
<i>I'm going to give it my all.</i>

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.260
<b>Achiga Girls'</b>

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.150
I'm back.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.630
Good work, Arata-chan.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.430
Nice job!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.650
Good job.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.860
Good job, Captain.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.520
You did well, Arata.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.580
Matano-senpai!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.240
Oohoshi...

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:14.120
Thanks for that handicap!

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.330
As ruthless as always.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.230
I've never seen you lose that many points.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.900
I got played bigtime.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.920
Bigtime?

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.380
Yup.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:30.500
But if you lose too, I'll be in an even 
more precarious position than I am now.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.980
So please, go out there and win.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.450
'Kay.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.540
I was going to do that anyway.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.870
There's no way I will lose.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.780
<b>Senriyama Girls'</b>

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.780
I'm back.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:44.880
Hey.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.680
Where's Shimizudani-senpai?

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.030
She's going straight to the 
game from the hospital.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.030
You think it's okay?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.060
What, exactly?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.010
Well...

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.570
<i>Shimizudani-senpai's a third year.</i>

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.540
<i>They transform during the Interhigh games.</i>

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:01.170
<i>And, unlike the second round match, 
she'll probably be more offensive.</i>

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.920
<i>And furthermore...</i>

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.170
<i>She's worried about Onjouji-senpai, too.</i>

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.290
<i>Toki...</i>

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.920
<i>The first match of the semifinals</i>

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.020
<i>is at last entering the fifth players' match!</i>

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.770
<i>Only two schools will be 
moving on to the finals!</i>

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:22.770
Everything now rests on the 
shoulders of these four players!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:30.780
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
 2nd Year - Fifth Player
 Tsuruta Himeko

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.080
The Kyuushuu powerhouse: Shindouji.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.200
Their anchor works in a combo with 
Shirouzu Mairu, as double aces.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.780
Can Tsuruta Himeko complete the combo?

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:37.710
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
 3rd Year - Fifth Player
 Shimizudani Ryuuka

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.240
You all know Senriyama Girls' 
captain, Shimizudani Ryuuka!

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.710
She tops the Kansai region 
in average points earned!

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:44.960
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
 1st Year - Fifth Player
 Takakamo Shizuno

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.810
Back at Interhigh semifinals 
for the first time in ten years,

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.160
we've got Achiga Girls'!

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.820
She's not wearing a tracksuit today, folks!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:44.960
It's Takakamo Shizuno!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:54.470
Shiraitodai High (West Tokyo)
 1st Year - Fifth Player
 Oohoshi Awai

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:48.140
The only first year from the 
reigning champions, Shiraitodai.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.900
The supernova who appeared out of nowhere,

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.450
they're even calling her the 
successor to Miyanaga Teru:

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.470
Oohoshi Awai!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.720
It's finally time for the decisive match!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.540
The game will now begin!

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:15.950
<i>Man, these tiles are awful!</i>

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.120
<i>I'm six tiles from tenpai.</i>

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.590
It really is here! She's starting 
five tiles from tenpai!

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:23.130
Everybody except Oohoshi's 
starting hand is terrible!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.670
Everyone's five or six 
tiles away from tenpai!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.420
It even works on Ryuuka.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.340
That's amazing.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.420
<i>Ever since</i>

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.400
the regional preliminaries,

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.350
many of Oohoshi's opponents 
have started with slow hands!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.970
One relief is that the hands do 
develop normally after that.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.430
Oh, really?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.820
Even in our club, the only one

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.670
who can beat this is Takami, 
during the last hand.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:48.280
Shindouji did beat it a few times 
in the second round match.

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:51.070
Don't you think Awai 
was just holding back?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:54.500
<i>Yes!</i>

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>It's finally getting somewhere.</i>

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:57.910
Ron.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.720
5,200.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.060
Yes.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:06.500
<i>It's so unfair that she's the 
only one with a quick hand.</i>

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.070
<i>East Hand 2.</i>

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.750
<i>I'm lucky that I'm dealer.</i>

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.510
<i>Should I take a chance?</i>

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:14.950
<i>I will!</i>

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:21.830
Pon.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:24.600
<i>Now here...</i>

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:29.480
Chi.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:30.650
<i>I have to get...</i>

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:31.690
Pon.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:36.280
Tsumo!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.840
500 from everyone.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:38.850
<i>A fast win.</i>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.210
Marvelous!

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.280
<i>Himeko...</i>

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.170
East Hand 2

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.170
Bonus 1

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.050
<i>The mangan key.</i>

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:14.070
<i>The mangan is here.</i>

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.640
Two tiles from tenpai!

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.100
It's been broken.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:20.830
Huh?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.830
I guess their combined power surpasses Awai's.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.330
They both have high individual ability, too.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:30.590
Ron.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.510
12,300.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.670
<i>With a closed hand on turn 4?</i>

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.240
<i>But my Perfect Safety Zone is...</i>

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.250
I can't believe it.

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:47.390
<i>Nice! You're pretty good!</i>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.200
<i>Shindouji!</i>

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.480
East Hand 2

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.480
Bonus 2

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.990
They didn't have a

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.580
second bonus hand last match, 
so this doesn't matter too much.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:56.740
It doesn't?

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:58.910
Ron!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.510
3,200.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:03.620
This is the problem.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:05.880
<i>East Hand 3.</i>

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.470
<i>The baiman is coming.</i>

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.680
<i>East Hand 3. Akado-sensei 
told me to be careful here.</i>

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.560
<i>I'm looking forward to the baiman.</i>

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.770
<i>Come. Become a baiman!</i>

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.550
<i>Of course I have to be dealer now...</i>

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:58.300
<i>I look forward to the baiman, but...</i>

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.050
Chi!

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.300
<i>I also want to try stopping it.</i>

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.860
<i>It's great having so much to look forward to!</i>

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:11.650
<i>Shiraitodai's Oohoshi Awai is really strong.</i>

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.460
<i>She was really wreaking havoc
in the second round match.</i>

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:19.650
<i>It's no surprise she's been tasked as 
their fifth player, even as a first year.</i>

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.590
<i>However!</i>

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:23.660
<i>She wasn't able to stop 
our combo even once!</i>

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:25.740
Riichi.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:30.120
<i>Our bond cannot be broken! 
Just try to break it!</i>

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.840
<i>Do you alone have...</i>

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.840
<i>as much as we...</i>

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:42.810
<i>have built up?!</i>

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:47.510
Tsumo!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.010
4,000. 8,000.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.250
<i>It really is a baiman!</i>

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:56.350
<i>They're making a comeback!</i>

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.830
<i>Shindouji's combo is strong.</i>

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.750
<i>I guess I'll give up trying 
to stop it, for now.</i>

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.240
She's unleashed a baiman!

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.240
Shindouji shoots from last place
to second, and is close to first!

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.250
<i>We've fallen to last place.</i>

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.150
<i>I'm sorry, Toki.</i>

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.760
<i>After entering Shiraitodai, 
it only took that first year</i>

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.310
<i>one month to become a regular 
player for their top team.</i>

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:23.240
<i>I knew she's not ordinary.</i>

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.010
<i>Plus Shindouji, with the enhanced 
firepower of their double aces...</i>

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:33.020
<i>If she won this baiman, she could win 
the second half's counted yakuman, too.</i>

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.900
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.160
<i>I might be in a little bit of trouble.</i>

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.540
<i>Ryuuka.</i>

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.630
<i>If only you were right here, Toki.</i>

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.990
<i>I think I could relax a bit.</i>

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.660
<i>Remember...</i>

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.160
<i>Ryuuka.</i>

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.060
<i>Ryuuka.</i>

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:57.880
<i>Toki...</i>

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:04.930
Toki...

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.200
Wanna go buy something to drink?

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.560
You really like sleeping 
in people's laps, huh?

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:16.730
There's a totally serious reason for this.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.000
Huh?

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.970
I mean, with weird abilities 
like seeing ahead one turn,

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:26.200
it's better if a naturally strong player, 
like you, has that kind of power.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:30.870
So I do this to try to send 
some of that power to you.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.080
So that's why you rest 
your head on my lap!

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.460
No need to thank me.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:43.210
<i>Later, when I tried to think about 
it rationally, I was like, "Huh?"</i>

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.720
<i>Even thinking about it now, 
my reaction is the same.</i>

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:49.120
<i>That's right, Ryuuka.</i>

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.470
<i>I can feel Toki here.</i>

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.990
<i>We're not alone, either!</i>

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.290
<i>I'll show you the future.</i>

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.010
<i>I saw it!</i>

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.870
She's discarding the south?

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.750
If she's throwing away honor tiles, 
you'd start with the north.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.190
You mean digitally?

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.450
Yeah, a chanta is possible,

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.450
(Chanta: Terminal or honor in each set)

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.670
and since you call it, keeping your 
own wind would make sense.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.680
Wait, she discarded the two of characters?!

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.340
Shouldn't she have gone with 
the previously discarded north?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.970
This is a different sequence 
than we've seen before.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:19.860
<i>Shimizudani Ryuuka tops Kansai in 
highest average points earned</i>

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.360
<i>due to her precise plays and 
highly accurate predictions.</i>

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:26.200
<i>Something's going to happen in this hand.</i>

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:36.700
Ron!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.520
12,000.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.170
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:45.790
<i>My hand was just like in the vision.</i>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.390
<i>I was watching for whether Tsuruhime 
would win in East Round 4.</i>

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:50.430
<i>How did this happen?</i>

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.540
<i>I didn't get a key for this hand...</i>

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.170
<i>Her starting tiles didn't seem like 
a hand anyone could win with.</i>

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.070
The champion is dethroned!

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.770
Shiraitodai, who was in first place 
since the first players' match,

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.730
has fallen straight to last place!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.530
The scores suggest that this is a close race,

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.230
but looking just at these players, 
Shindouji's overwhelming!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:11.130
You mean, if they keep it up,

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.530
Shindouji will come out on top?

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:16.530
I'm sure there are some 
big wins still ahead.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.790
<i>It's just like Toki showed me.</i>

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.360
<i>Will it always be exactly like I saw it?</i>

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:26.360
<i>If you see it, you will definitely win it.</i>

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:29.050
<i>That's the Pillow God Toki-chan's revelation.</i>

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:29.570
<b>East</b>

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:29.960
<b>South</b>

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:33.860
<i>Unlike Toki, I can see how I will win,</i>

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:36.220
<i>but I can't see anybody else's hand.</i>

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.210
<i>I'm dealer... I want to win this one.</i>

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:44.820
<i>Toki!</i>

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.480
<i>Huh?</i>

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.980
<i>See ya!</i>

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.490
<i>What?! Hey!</i>

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.240
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:59.110
<i>This is the South Hand 1 that 
Shirouzu Mairu won before.</i>

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.000
<i>It happened in that hand too,</i>

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:04.000
<i>but now something is 
fundamentally different here.</i>

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:05.750
<i>In this hand,</i>

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.000
<i>their combo is active!</i>

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:11.840
Tsumo!

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:13.850
3,000. 6,000.

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.340
<i>So it is happening that way...</i>

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:19.080
Marvelous!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.280
Shindouji's got a haneman tsumo!

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.860
At one point, they were 
down to 30,000 points,

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:26.310
but a-ma-zing-ly, Shindouji is now in the lead!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:29.010
It's just like pro player Kokaji predicted!

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:31.790
Not only is she Japan's best; 
she also makes the best predictions!

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:33.510
There is no connection there!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.610
South Hand 2

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.610
Dealer - Tsuruta Himeko

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.940
<i>That was a short stay at the top.</i>

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.010
<i>That's right.</i>

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:39.680
<i>To—</i>

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.340
<i>Look what comes next.</i>

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.250
<i>A kuitan?</i>

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.380
<i>That's not worth much...</i>

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:51.070
<i>That's this hand's best.</i>

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.200
<i>So you're saying I always see the best?</i>

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.640
<i>Not the best, but the highest 
scoring winning hand.</i>

00:17:56.610 --> 00:18:00.050
<i>There might be other winning 
hands, but you only see that one.</i>

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.060
<i>Isn't it getting more and more restrictive?</i>

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:05.560
<i>Don't mix up the sequence.</i>

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.190
<i>Okay.</i>

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.580
<i>Bye bye!</i>

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:09.260
<i>If you say so...</i>

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:10.560
Ron.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:12.940
1,000.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:13.980
Okay.

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:15.370
<i>So cheap.</i>

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:16.820
<i>Why?</i>

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.980
<i>Why can these two win this much?</i>

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:29.220
<i>I guess it's better than not 
winning at all... I think.</i>

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.110
<i>Not sure about that.</i>

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.480
<i>You're so restless.</i>

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.970
<i>Can't you just stay here?</i>

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:35.780
<i>That's not going to work.</i>

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:36.880
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.050
<i>However nice and full your thighs may be,</i>

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:43.130
<i>there's a limit to how much 
power I can store there.</i>

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:46.040
<i>I can come about two more times.</i>

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.710
<i>So if I gained a little weight...</i>

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:48.830
<i>Don't do that!</i>

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.270
<i>You see a mangan for this hand.</i>

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:57.070
<i>All right!</i>

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>Now, just follow the directions closely</i>

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.160
<i>and use your Toki-chan with care.</i>

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:06.100
<i>Toki...</i>

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.620
South Hand 3

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.620
Dealer - Takakamo Shizuno

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:11.310
Tsumo!

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:12.700
2,000. 4,000.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.210
<i>Two more times, huh.</i>

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.040
<i>I don't care if you're the best in Kansai,</i>

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:24.220
<i>or the best in North Kyuushuu.</i>

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:27.930
<i>With you winning like this over and over,</i>

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.730
<i>I don't think I can take it much longer.</i>

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:33.980
<i>I can do it now, right?</i>

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.030
Awai means business.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.830
Too bad that we couldn't 
keep it until the finals.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.750
She's hardly done this, even 
during practice games at school.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:52.960
I guess that means these 
players must be that strong.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:58.550
Riichi.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.890
<i>Double riichi?!</i>

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.970
This is pretty bad...

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:09.930
Oohoshi Awai has a double riichi!

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.910
Compared to the slow hands of the 
other three, this is overwhelming!

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:16.050
But her hand is only worth a double riichi!

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.050
Hopefully that's all it is.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:18.610
Huh?

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:21.520
This is the first time this has 
happened in a public game.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.190
No... she used it once in the regional.

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:26.480
In the second half of the finals.

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:27.250
Oh...

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.870
The reason for that was...

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:33.700
I just didn't want to lose to Takami 
in terms of total points won.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.130
It's fine if it's Teru though.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.210
Remember?

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:41.520
I doubt there are many players who
 have connected that one hand to this.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.720
Even if there are some, Awai won't lose.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.510
<i>Shizu, you know, right?</i>

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:52.980
<i>Oohoshi Awai-san's double riichi.</i>

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.730
<i>The one Akado-sensei talked about!</i>

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.570
<i>Shizu, be careful when Oohoshi 
Awai goes for a double riichi.</i>

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.870
<i>Double riichi? Why?</i>

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.380
<i>Oohoshi Awai is a supernova 
who just appeared this year,</i>

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:11.900
<i>so there are few records of her.</i>

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:15.340
<i>However, I can't believe that 
a first year would become a</i>

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:17.550
<i>regular just because she can 
delay other players' hands.</i>

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:18.880
<i>That's powerful enough!</i>

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.590
<i>No, at Shiraitodai, they 
have multiple teams.</i>

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.760
<i>The team that wins their internal 
competition goes to the tournaments.</i>

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:31.520
<i>So the top five of Shiraitodai won't 
necessarily be the representatives.</i>

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:35.020
<i>Each of those teams follows 
a different concept,</i>

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:38.310
<i>and Miyanaga Teru's team 
specializes in attacking.</i>

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:40.560
<i>Then that means...</i>

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>Yes.</i>

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.490
<i>Oohoshi Awai is also an offensive player.</i>

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:47.320
<i>So she's hiding her fangs?</i>

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.740
<i>Why should I pay attention 
to that one double riichi?</i>

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:53.700
<i>The West Tokyo tournament 
had great equipment.</i>

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:58.110
<i>They have continuous footage of 
just each player's expression.</i>

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:02.130
<i>That's Shouan Girls' Academy's fifth 
player at the West Tokyo regional.</i>

00:22:02.770 --> 00:22:06.130
<i>This video is from her match against 
Oohoshi Awai in the finals.</i>

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:08.990
<i>This girl did quite well.</i>

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:12.060
<i>Her scores in the individual 
tournament were amazing, too.</i>

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.210
<i>Watch in about three seconds.</i>

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:19.190
<i>Huh? What? Eek, that's scary!</i>

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:20.110
<i>See?</i>

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:24.110
<i>That's right before Oohoshi Awai 
declares her double riichi.</i>

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:27.450
<i>Not when she declares 
it, or when she wins?</i>

00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:30.890
<i>So that means she sensed something?</i>

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:33.910
<i>This is just my guess,</i>

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:36.410
<i>but once Oohoshi Awai 
declares double riichi,</i>

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:39.230
<i>there are a few things you 
need to watch out for.</i>

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:40.710
<i>The first one is...</i>

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:42.380
Kan!

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:43.780
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:50.010
<i>If I wanted to go for it, 
I'd discard what I drew....</i>

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:53.560
<i>Only discard a 100% safe tile after a kan.</i>

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:57.100
<i>It's the last hand, I'm in last, 
and I haven't won a hand, but...</i>

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:09.310
<i>Tenpai...</i>

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:12.250
<i>The 8 of bamboo are a wall,</i>

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:13.990
<i>then it's either I wait to pair 
a title or triple one of two titles.</i>

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:17.280
<i>I don't like the idea of Oohoshi 
continuing to be dealer...</i>

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:19.030
<i>There are no safe tiles left anyway.</i>

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:23.670
<i>I'm keeping my tenpai!</i>

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:25.760
Ron.

00:23:28.180 --> 00:23:29.380
<i>A reverse spin?!</i>

00:23:31.310 --> 00:23:33.390
<i>Phew, it's only the double riichi.</i>

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:42.020
<i>Kan dora?!</i>

00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:44.960
18,000!

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:49.010
A direct 18 hit!

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.780
Shiraitodai has taken back the throne!

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:55.030
<i>If I hadn't backed down,
 I would have dealt into that!</i>

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:59.550
There was a win like this before, just once!

00:23:59.550 --> 00:24:00.460
Really?

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.290
Shizu-chan...

00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:04.880
So it's decided...

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.380
I don't intend to stop being the dealer.

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:13.010
South Hand 4

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:13.010
Dealer - Oohoshi Awai
Bonus 1

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:16.930
Riichi.

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.560
<i>Double riichi, again?!</i>

00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:21.250
She declares double riichi again!

00:24:21.250 --> 00:24:25.190
This time it's also just 
a double riichi. For now.

00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:27.920
<i>I'm five tiles from tenpai</i>

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:29.740
<i>while the dealer has repeated double riichis.</i>

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:32.360
<i>However, if I can only call 
Toki two more times,</i>

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:34.350
<i>I'd like to save those for when 
I'm dealer in the second half.</i>

00:24:36.810 --> 00:24:39.410
<i>Even without a key, I'll end her 
dealer turn with my own power!</i>

00:24:46.110 --> 00:24:48.020
What did the dice show?

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:49.470
Um...

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:51.970
Right 2, I think.

00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:53.220
Snake eyes?

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:55.220
That's great.

00:24:55.840 --> 00:25:00.270
Whether Shizu can fight Oohoshi 
Awai will be decided this hand!

00:25:02.760 --> 00:25:03.440
Kan.

00:25:03.940 --> 00:25:09.150
If my prediction is right, Oohoshi 
will win in the next few turns.

00:25:09.150 --> 00:25:10.440
Seriously?

00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:13.150
Turn 15

00:25:11.570 --> 00:25:14.980
Nothing has happened and it's turn 16...

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:16.410
Huh?!

00:25:16.410 --> 00:25:18.420
Well, that happens sometimes.

00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:20.700
There's little data on Oohoshi Awai.

00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:22.410
<i>That's weird.</i>

00:25:27.310 --> 00:25:29.340
<i>This is strange.</i>

00:25:30.690 --> 00:25:31.510
Ron.

00:25:33.940 --> 00:25:34.760
<i>Huh?</i>

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:40.810
7,700 with the bonus is 8,000.

00:25:41.580 --> 00:25:42.760
<i>Achiga Girls'?!</i>

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:47.110
<i>What... was her name again?</i>

00:25:47.940 --> 00:25:49.110
This girl...

00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:52.280
is Achiga Girls' fifth player?

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:53.490
Yes.

00:25:54.450 --> 00:25:56.240
That's Takakamo Shizuno.

00:25:56.980 --> 00:25:59.990
The first half is over!

00:25:59.990 --> 00:26:02.220
Achiga Girls' Takakamo Shizuno strikes the top

00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:04.620
and escapes from the yakitori penalty!

00:26:04.620 --> 00:26:08.390
All that's left in this match of the semifinals is 
the second half of the fifth players' match!

00:26:08.390 --> 00:26:09.500
<i>What was with that hand?</i>

00:26:10.160 --> 00:26:11.890
<i>Did she do something?</i>

00:26:12.620 --> 00:26:16.430
<i>Does that just mean that Oohoshi's 
Awai's control isn't all that?</i>

00:26:17.020 --> 00:26:21.670
When we played against Shizuno for 
the first time about two months ago,

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:24.060
I could already hear the footsteps.

00:26:24.830 --> 00:26:26.940
The first day of our training 
matches against Achiga,

00:26:27.670 --> 00:26:30.410
Koromo won three times 
with a haitei raoyue.

00:26:27.670 --> 00:26:30.410
(Haitei raoyue: winning on the last draw from the wall)

00:26:31.010 --> 00:26:33.760
However, Koromo had planned 
to do that five times.

00:26:35.510 --> 00:26:40.240
By the second day, she couldn't 
even get to the last tile.

00:26:44.910 --> 00:26:46.950
Why are you so worn down?

00:26:48.170 --> 00:26:49.230
Ako!

00:26:49.230 --> 00:26:50.210
Here,

00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:51.880
get some sugar in you.

00:26:51.880 --> 00:26:52.790
Thank you.

00:26:55.680 --> 00:26:57.840
Harue says you can stay like this.

00:26:58.370 --> 00:26:59.140
Yeah.

00:27:00.650 --> 00:27:02.080
I kinda thought so.

00:27:03.750 --> 00:27:05.950
Just one more East-South match...

00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:08.370
You mean 11, don't you?

00:27:08.770 --> 00:27:09.950
I hope so.

00:27:12.540 --> 00:27:17.700
The commercials are over! 
Meet back in front of the TV!

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:20.240
If you keep dissing the commercials like that,

00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:22.530
you're going to get in trouble 
with the sponsors again.

00:27:22.530 --> 00:27:24.120
Please forgive this lowly 
station announcer!

00:27:24.900 --> 00:27:26.580
Freelancers can't do that, either!

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:29.870
If I get fired, take responsibility 
and look after me, okay?

00:27:30.490 --> 00:27:34.590
Huh? Uh, okay... Wait, why 
is it my responsibility?!

00:27:34.990 --> 00:27:37.610
Just now, we got sidetracked because 
of pro player Kokaji, again.

00:27:38.170 --> 00:27:40.810
Finally, it's the second half 
of the fifth players' match!

00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:47.980
The battle for the right to go to 
the finals is reaching its climax!

00:27:48.270 --> 00:27:49.480
Achiga Girls' (Nara)
 1st year - Fifth Player
 Takakamo Shizuno

00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:51.730
There's only one East-South match left!

00:27:50.480 --> 00:27:51.730
Shiraitodai High (West Tokyo)
 1st Year - Fifth Player
 Oohoshi Awai

00:27:51.730 --> 00:27:56.220
The final game that will decide the fate 
of twenty people is about to begin!

00:27:52.520 --> 00:27:53.980
Shindouji Girls' (Fukuoka)
 2nd year - Fifth Player
 Tsuruta Himeko

00:27:55.020 --> 00:27:56.480
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
 3rd year - Fifth Player
 Shimizudani Ryuuka

00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:04.610
Ryuuka...

00:28:16.210 --> 00:28:20.450
And... The game begins!

00:29:43.090 --> 00:29:58.580
<b>The Path</b>

00:29:46.100 --> 00:29:48.230
Shizu, what are you running 
for all of a sudden?

00:29:48.230 --> 00:29:51.430
When I remembered the mountains
 of Yoshino, my body got all restless!

00:29:52.420 --> 00:29:55.570
Oh, be careful! 
That path follows a cliff!

00:29:55.570 --> 00:29:56.850
Whoa, that was close!
